// Test-suite type-check configuration.
//
// Extends the project root so the specs stay under the same `strict` family
// as the library, with two of the index-signature guards relaxed. Both are
// load-bearing for src/ (they catch dynamic option-object lookups) and
// actively hostile to tests, which traverse a parsed XML tree whose keys are
// only known at runtime:
//
//   noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature — a parsed tree is accessed as
//     `result.root.tag['@_id']`. Without this rule, the leading `result.root`
//     dot access is allowed; with it, every traversal step would have to be
//     rewritten to bracket form purely to satisfy the checker.
//
//   noUncheckedIndexedAccess — a test asserting `result.item[0]['@_id']` is
//     checking that the parser produced the value. Making the type
//     `T | undefined` forces a null-check on every assertion, which would
//     obscure the thing under test behind type noise.
//
// The library keeps both rules (see the root tsconfig, which now covers
// src/ only). Only the test tree opts out, and only because its shape is
// genuinely dynamic.
//
// The two `src/*.d.ts` files are pulled in explicitly: they carry the module
// augmentations that correct stale declarations in `path-expression-matcher`
// and the `@nodable` builder packages. Without them the specs would see the
// published — and wrong — types, and the real classes would look
// unassignable to the parser's structural builder contract.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": { "noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature": false, "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false },
  "include": ["./**/*.ts", "../src/path-expression-matcher.d.ts", "../src/nodable-builders.d.ts"]
}
